Sphere light moving with the camera must not be motion blurred

The render delegate set the light transform with a single key, without sampling it over the
shutter interval like the other primitives do. A light moving with the camera was then static
in the scene while the camera moved, and it looked motion blurred in the render. The legacy
USD reader already sampled the light transform over the shutter.

The camera and the red sphere light are parented under an animated Xform, so the light must look
sharp. The white sphere doesn't move, so it's blurred by the camera motion.

See #2863 (ARNOLD-18309)

author: sebastien ortega

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda'}
